      <title>What Bessent's US Treasury Intervention Means for Stocks &amp; Mortgages | Daybreak Europe 8/20/2026</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/videos/2026-08-20/daybreak-europe-8-20-2026-video</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">e432a4291284a6a885bd5f91</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 07:01:49 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Bloomberg Daybreak Europe is your essential morning viewing to stay ahead. Live from London, we set the agenda for your day, catching you up with overnight markets news from the US and Asia. And we'll tell you what matters for investors in Europe, giving you insight before trading begins.

With a slew of unexpected maneuvers this year, Scott Bessent has emerged as the most interventionist Treasury secretary in financial markets in decades — putting his credibility on the line in an effort to quell a potentially damaging rise in US borrowing costs.

President Donald Trump announced plans to inflict what he called an “economic D-Day” against Iran, underscoring his frustration with the country’s refusal to capitulate despite weeks of strikes and a US blockade that’s crimped its oil exports.

And Bloomberg understands Banca Monte dei Paschi's board of directors is set to review strategic alternatives to Intesa Sanpaolo's takeover bid. (Source: Bloomberg)</description>
